    "body": "This is assuming that there is nothing except a selectedcontent element inside the button, right?\n\nWhat if I did this?\n```html\n<select>\n  <button>hello world</button>\n  <option>one</option>\n  <option>two</option>\n</select>\n```\nOr this:\n```html\n<select>\n  <button>\n    selected: <selectedcontent></selectedcontent>\n  </button>\n  <option>one</option>\n  <option>two</option>\n</select>\n```\nI know that maybe these cases aren't completely considered valid, but should we at least have some sort of affordance to make it more of a min-width/min-inline-size kind of thing where the button can grow to fit larger contents if the author provides larger contents? This paragraph as-is would clip the text in the button in these cases, right?",
    "created_at": "2026-10-09T18:24:46Z",
    "updated_at": "2026-10-09T18:25:28Z",
